      "findings": [
        "Main menu renders faithfully: NONOGRAM title, PICTURE LOGIC PUZZLE subtitle, star counter + LEVEL pill + hearts HUD, and all six buttons (PLAY / SELECT LEVEL / RANDOM PUZZLE / MULTIPLAYER / HOW TO PLAY / SETTINGS) — vision-verified against the exploration memory.",
        "PLAY opens the Level 1 game screen: 9x9 grid with column clues above and row clues left, hearts/stars HUD, x/42 progress counter and progress bar, FILL/X tool buttons at bottom — vision-verified.",
        "Cell fill toggling works: after measuring the board geometry (grid ~x190-897, y580-1445, center cell ~(543,1011)), repeated taps at the cell center each produced a distinct screen state, consistent with the yellow fill toggling on/off and the counter switching between 0/42 and 1/42.",
        "Pause button opens a PAUSED overlay (RESUME / RESTART LEVEL / MAIN MENU) and RESUME returns to the game — verified via screen transitions.",
        "SELECT LEVEL opens the level-select grid; locked level tiles do not navigate (tap on tile 2 was a no-op as designed); back arrow returns to menu.",
        "HOW TO PLAY, SETTINGS (toggle switch changed state on tap) and MULTIPLAYER (offline notice) screens all render and navigate correctly.",
        "Back navigation works on every screen; restart_app relaunches to the main menu with the LEVEL pill state persisted (SharedPreferences).",
        "No private or third-party content is included: all puzzle art, text and icons are synthetic/drawn in code."
      ],
